The ReSTIR story's worked example of RIS
========================================

What the story draws on the canvas (lab/src/math/) with render_lab's math library (`render_lab_math`): the worked
example of RIS (chapter 2, demos/toy.rs's numbers through the package's natives), stage by stage as its stage (`stepOf "toy" 23`, the clips below)
goes from 0 to 23. Each stage is one sentence's animation; `toyDrop` (or the counterfactual stages) removes a
part of W.

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* render_lab_math]
$[Import* paper_restir_values]
$[Import* paper_restir_natives]
$[Import* paper_restir_common]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* render_lab_math]
$[Import* paper_restir_values]
$[Import* paper_restir_natives]


Numbers

Fn([Int], String). Sample i's name.
$[# {_name i} {!if {= i 0} "A" "B"}]
Fn([Int], String). The cheap choice's probability of sample i, as a fraction.
$[# {_pLatex i} {fractionLatex {toyQuarters i} 4}]
Fn([Int, Int], String). Sample i's weight with `drop`, as a fraction.
$[# {_wLatex i drop} {rational {toyWeight i drop}}]

The stages

Fn([Float, Float, Float, Float], Float). A value that a removed part of W moves, at stage s: whole until stage 18,
then to its value without the average of the weights (`dropped2`), at stage 19 to its value without the division
by p (`dropped1`), and back at stage 21; outside the story's stages, as `toyDrop` removes a part.
$[# {_moving s whole dropped2 dropped1}
    [# {_by drop} {!if {= drop 2} dropped2 {!if {= drop 1} dropped1 whole}}]
    {!if {< s 18.0}
        {_by {round {toyDrop}}}
        {!if {< s 19.0}
            {lerp whole dropped2 {smooth {phase s 18.0 18.6}}}
            {!if {< s 21.0}
                {lerp dropped2 dropped1 {smooth {phase s 19.0 19.6}}}
                {!if {< s 22.0}
                    {lerp dropped1 whole {smooth {phase s 21.0 21.6}}}
                    {_by {round {toyDrop}}}}}}}]

Phase one: two samples, their p, p-hat, and w

Fn([Int], List(Mob)). Sample i's two bars, p's and p-hat's, each kind scaled to its larger value, labelled with
their values, and its name under them.
$[# {_barsOf i}
    [# x {!if {= i 0} -5.2 -2.8}]
    [# base -2.0]
    [# tall 2.6]
    [# p {/ {float {toyQuarters i}} 4.0}]
    [# target {toyBrings i}]
    [# pBox {box {v2 {- x 0.6} base} {v2 {- x 0.1} {+ base {* tall {/ p 0.75}}}}}]
    [# tBox {box {v2 {+ x 0.1} base} {v2 {+ x 0.6} {+ base {* tall {/ target 3.0}}}}}]
    [# pBar {filled f"{p${_name i}}" pBox pColor 0.9}]
    [# tBar {filled f"{t${_name i}}" tBox targetColor 0.9}]
    {flatten {'
        {moveTo {tex f"{n${_name i}}" {_name i} 0.5 textColor} {v2 x {- base 0.45}}}
        pBar
        {nextTo {tex f"{pv${_name i}}" {_pLatex i} 0.42 pColor} pBar up 0.12}
        tBar
        {nextTo {tex f"{tv${_name i}}" {str {round target}} 0.42 targetColor} tBar up 0.12}}}]
Fn([Int, String], List(Mob)). One piece of sample i's bars by the start of its name: `n` its name, `p` and `t`
its bars, `pv` and `tv` their labels.
$[# {_barPiece i kind} {withId {_barsOf i} {++ kind {_name i}}}]
Fn([Int], List(ScorePart)). Sample i's bars as the first sentences build them: its name, then p's bar and label,
then p-hat's; all leave when the square of the lists takes their place.
$[# {_barParts i}
    [# {_piece kind at length how} {part
        {++ kind {_name i}}
        {^ {s} {_barPiece i kind}}
        {' {enterOver at length how} {exit 7.0}}}]
    {'
        {_piece "n" 0.0 1.0 fadeIn}
        {_piece "p" 1.0 0.8 growUp}
        {_piece "pv" 1.5 0.5 fadeIn}
        {_piece "t" 2.0 0.8 growUp}
        {_piece "tv" 2.5 0.5 fadeIn}}]
Fn([], List(ScorePart)). The key to the bars: p in the cheap choice's colour, and p-hat, which stage 3 writes
equal to f.
$[# {_legendParts}
    [# p {append
        {filled "keyP" {box {v2 -6.4 3.0} {v2 -6.1 3.3}} pColor 0.9}
        {moveTo {tex "keyPText" "p" 0.42 pColor} {v2 -5.75 3.15}}}]
    [# t {append
        {filled "keyT" {box {v2 -4.9 3.0} {v2 -4.6 3.3}} targetColor 0.9}
        {moveTo {tex "keyTText" f"{\hat p}" 0.42 targetColor} {v2 -4.25 3.19}}}]
    [# eq {moveTo {tex "keyF" f"{= f}" 0.42 targetColor} {v2 -3.55 3.15}}]
    {'
        {part "keyP" {^ {s} p} {' {enter 1.0 fadeIn} {exit 7.0}}}
        {part "keyT" {^ {s} t} {' {enter 2.0 fadeIn} {exit 7.0}}}
        {part "keyF" {^ {s} eq} {' {enterOver 3.0 1.0 write} {exit 7.0}}}}]
Fn([], List(ScorePart)). The true total: copies of the two p-hat bars flown into one column, 1 and 3, braced as 4.
$[# {_totalParts}
    [# x -0.7]
    [# base -2.0]
    [# unit {/ 2.6 3.0}]
    [# a {filled "totalA" {box {v2 {- x 0.25} base} {v2 {+ x 0.25} {+ base unit}}} targetColor 0.9}]
    [# b {filled "totalB"
        {box {v2 {- x 0.25} {+ base unit}} {v2 {+ x 0.25} {+ base {* 4.0 unit}}}}
        targetColor
        0.9}]
    [# outline {outlined "totalOutline" {boxOf {append a b}} totalColor 3.0}]
    [# label {tex "totalValue" {str {round {+ {toyBrings 0} {toyBrings 1}}}} 0.5 totalColor}]
    [# braced {braceLabel "totalBrace" {append a b} right 0.12 totalColor label}]
    [# {_flown i} {^ {t f} {fromCopy t {_barPiece i "t"} f}}]
    {'
        {part "totalA" {^ {s} a} {' {enter 4.0 {_flown 0}} {exit 7.0}}}
        {part "totalB" {^ {s} b} {' {enter 4.2 {_flown 1}} {exit 7.0}}}
        {part "totalBrace"
            {^ {s} {append outline braced}}
            {' {enterOver 4.6 0.4 create} {exit 7.0}}}}]

The table of the samples' p, p-hat, and w

Fn([Int], Table). The table of the samples' p, p-hat, and w (with `drop`), centred on the origin.
$[# {_table drop}
    [# header {'
        {words "h0" "" 0.42 textColor}
        {tex "hp" "p" 0.42 pColor}
        {tex "ht" f"{\hat p}" 0.42 targetColor}
        {texParts "hw" f"{w = \frac{\lit{1}{\hat p}}{\lit{2}{p}}}" 0.42 weightColor
            {' "hwt" "hwp"}
            {' targetColor pColor}}}]
    [# {_row i} {'
        {tex f"{r${_name i}}" {_name i} 0.42 textColor}
        {tex f"{c${_name i}p}" {_pLatex i} 0.42 pColor}
        {tex f"{c${_name i}t}" {str {round {toyBrings i}}} 0.42 targetColor}
        {tex f"{c${_name i}w}" {_wLatex i drop} 0.42 weightColor}}]
    {table "table" {' header {_row 0} {_row 1}} 0.14 textDimColor}]
Fn([Int], Table). The table where it is written, beside the bars.
$[# {_tableBeside drop} {tableShifted {_table drop} {v2 3.8 0.4}}]
Fn([Int], Table). The table in the top right corner, where it waits while the lists are worked out.
$[# {_tableAside drop}
    [# t {_table drop}]
    [# b {boxOf {tableFigure t}}]
    {tableShifted t {v2 {- {- {/ canvasWidth 2.0} 0.2} {.x {.hi b}}} {- 3.95 {.y {.hi b}}}}}]
Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The table written as stage 5 runs (`t` 0 to 1): its rules and names, then p and p-hat
flying from the bars' labels into their cells, then the weights.
$[# {_tableIn t}
    [# s {+ 5.0 t}]
    [# tb {_tableBeside 0}]
    [# {_fly k i kind cell} {fromCopy
        {phase s {+ 5.0 {* 0.1 {float k}}} {+ 5.4 {* 0.1 {float k}}}}
        {_barPiece i kind}
        cell}]
    {flatten {'
        {create {phase s 5.0 5.3} {.rules tb}}
        {write {phase s 5.0 5.4} {append {rowOf tb 0} {append {cellOf tb 1 0} {cellOf tb 2 0}}}}
        {_fly 0 0 "pv" {cellOf tb 1 1}}
        {_fly 1 0 "tv" {cellOf tb 1 2}}
        {_fly 2 1 "pv" {cellOf tb 2 1}}
        {_fly 3 1 "tv" {cellOf tb 2 2}}
        {write {phase s 5.5 5.8} {cellOf tb 1 3}}
        {write {phase s 5.7 6.0} {cellOf tb 2 3}}}}]
Fn([], ScorePart). The table: written at stage 5, B's weight pointed at in stage 6, moved aside at 7; in stages
19 to 21, p struck out of w (its weights then without the division) and B's weight pointed at; it fades out
as stage 22 begins.
$[# {_tableParts}
    [# {_fig drop} {^ {s} {tableFigure {_tableAside drop}}}]
    [# {_point ids} {^ {t f} {pointParts t f ids accentColor}}]
    {'
        {part "table"
            {^ {s} {tableFigure {_tableBeside 0}}}
            {'
                {enterOver 5.0 1.0 {^ {t f} {_tableIn t}}}
                {emphasize 6.0 7.0 {_point {' "cBw"}}}
                {becomeOver 7.0 0.8 {_fig 0}}
                {hold 19.0 21.0 {^ {t f} {crossParts t f {' "hwp"} pColor}}}
                {becomeOver 19.2 0.5 {_fig 1}}
                {emphasize 20.0 21.0 {_point {' "cBw"}}}
                {exitOver 21.0 0.6 fadeOut}}}}]

Phase two: two candidates, every list, and their average

The square of the lists, where the bars were: across, the first candidate (A three quarters of the width, B the
rest); down, the second.
$[# _square [% {box {v2 -6.3 -3.4} {v2 -1.8 1.1}}]]
Fn([], List(Float)). The cheap choice's shares, A's then B's.
$[# {_shares} {map {' 0 1} {^ {i} {/ {float {toyQuarters i}} 4.0}}}]
The ink of a label on a lit cell: dark, so it reads on the bright fills in every theme.
$[# _onFill [% {rgb "#15161e"}]]
Fn([String, Color], List(Mob)). The square's cells, named `id` and coloured.
$[# {_cells id color} {areaSquare id {_shares} {_shares} _square {' color} 0.05}]
Fn([], List(Mob)). The square, its cells dim, the first candidate named above it and the second beside it.
$[# {_squareFigure}
    [# cells {_cells "sq" [% {rgb "#3b4150"}]}]
    [# names {flatten {map
        {' 0 1}
        {^ {i}
            [# c {boxCenter {boxOf {withId cells f"{sq.${str i}.${str i}}"}}}]
            {append
                {moveTo {tex f"{xa${_name i}}" {_name i} 0.42 textDimColor} {v2 {.x c} 1.5}}
                {moveTo {tex f"{xb${_name i}}" {_name i} 0.42 textDimColor} {v2 -6.7 {.y c}}}}}}}]
    {append cells names}]
Fn([Int, Int], String). The cell of the square where the first candidate is i and the second j.
$[# {_cell i j} f"{${str i}.${str j}}"]
Fn([Int], List({first: Int, second: Int})). The cells of list k (A A, A B or B A, B B).
$[# {_cellsOf k} {!if {= k 0}
    {' {pair 0 0}}
    {!if {= k 1} {' {pair 0 1} {pair 1 0}} {' {pair 1 1}}}}]
Fn([Int, Float], List(ScorePart)). List k's cells lit over the square's from stage `from`, then each labelled with
its chance in sixteenths (as the narration counts them: an A and a B, in either order, are 3 and 3 of the 6).
$[# {_listParts k from}
    [# lit {_cells "lit" estimateColor}]
    [# {_one c}
        [# id {_cell {.first c} {.second c}}]
        [# chance {* {toyQuarters {.first c}} {toyQuarters {.second c}}}]
        [# cell {faded {withId lit {++ "lit." id}} 0.85}]
        [# label {moveTo
            {tex {++ "chance." id} f"{\tfrac{${str chance}}{16}}" 0.42 _onFill}
            {boxCenter {boxOf cell}}}]
        {pair cell label}]
    [# ones {map {_cellsOf k} _one}]
    {'
        {part f"{lit${str k}}"
            {^ {s} {flatten {map ones {^ {o} {.first o}}}}}
            {' {enterOver from 0.4 create} {exit 22.0}}}
        {part f"{chance${str k}}"
            {^ {s} {flatten {map ones {^ {o} {.second o}}}}}
            {' {enterOver {+ from 0.3} 0.4 fadeIn} {exit 22.0}}}}]

The estimate of one list, as symbols and with each list's numbers: f(y)/p-hat(y) (1 here, as p-hat = f) times the
average of the two weights.
$[# _estimateCenter [% {v2 2.6 -0.2}]]
$[# {_estimateSymbols} {moveTo
    {texParts "est" f"{\lit{1}{\frac{f(y)}{\hat p(y)}} \cdot \frac{\lit{2}{w_1} + \lit{3}{w_2}}{\lit{4}{M}}}" 0.5 textColor
        {' "fp" "w1" "w2" "M"}
        {' targetColor weightColor weightColor textColor}}
    _estimateCenter}]
Fn([Int], List(Mob)). List k's estimate with its numbers.
$[# {_estimateNumbers k}
    [# l {nth {toyLists} k}]
    [# value {toyEstimate k 0}]
    [# w1 {_wLatex {.a l} 0}]
    [# w2 {_wLatex {.b l} 0}]
    {moveTo
        {texParts "est" f"{\lit{1}{1} \cdot \frac{\lit{2}{$w1} + \lit{3}{$w2}}{\lit{4}{2}} = \lit{5}{${rational value}}}" 0.5 textColor
            {' "fp" "w1" "w2" "M" "value"}
            {' targetColor weightColor weightColor textColor estimateColor}}
        _estimateCenter}]
The average over the lists, each estimate times its chance, which is the true total.
$[# {_averageFormula}
    [# l {toyLists}]
    {moveTo
        {texParts "avg" f"{\tfrac{${str {.sixteenths {nth l 0}}}}{16} \cdot \lit{1}{${rational {toyEstimate 0 0}}} + \tfrac{${str {.sixteenths {nth l 1}}}}{16} \cdot \lit{2}{${rational {toyEstimate 1 0}}} + \tfrac{${str {.sixteenths {nth l 2}}}}{16} \cdot \lit{3}{${rational {toyEstimate 2 0}}} = \lit{4}{${rational {toyAverage 0}}}}" 0.46 textColor
            {' "e0" "e1" "e2" "avgValue"}
            {' estimateColor estimateColor estimateColor totalColor}}
        _estimateCenter}]

The number line of the estimates, 0 to 12, under the formulas.
$[# _lineRange [% {axisRange 0.0 12.0 2.0}]]
$[# _lineA [% {v2 -1.4 -2.9}]]
$[# _lineB [% {v2 6.6 -2.9}]]
Fn([Float], Vec2). Where the estimate x is on the line.
$[# {_onLine x} {onLine _lineRange _lineA _lineB x}]
Fn([Int, Float], List(Mob)). List k's estimate as a dot on the line, the size of its chance, at its value as far
as a removed part has moved it at stage s.
$[# {_dot k s}
    [# chance {/ {float {.sixteenths {nth {toyLists} k}}} 16.0}]
    [# value {_moving s {toyEstimate k 0} {toyEstimate k 2} {toyEstimate k 1}}]
    {dotAt f"{dot${str k}}" {_onLine value} {+ 0.07 {* 0.3 {sqrt chance}}} estimateColor}]
Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The three estimates' dots at stage s.
$[# {_dots s} {flatten {map {' 0 1 2} {^ {k} {_dot k s}}}}]
Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The brace over the dots: the estimates' spread.
$[# {_spread s} {braceLabel "spread"
    {_dots s}
    up
    0.2
    estimateColor
    {tex "spreadText" f"{${rational {toyEstimate 0 0}} \ldots ${rational {toyEstimate 2 0}}}" 0.42
        estimateColor}}]
Fn([], List(Mob)). The true total's mark at 4, above the line.
$[# {_truth}
    [# truth {_onLine {toyAverage 0}}]
    {append
        {dashedLine "truth" {add2 truth {v2 0.0 0.9}} {sub2 truth {v2 0.0 0.08}} totalColor 2.5}
        {moveTo
            {tex "truthValue" {rational {toyAverage 0}} 0.42 totalColor}
            {add2 truth {v2 0.0 1.15}}}}]
Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The average's marker under the line's labels at stage s: sliding from 0 to the average in stage 14
(to where a removed part moves it later).
$[# {_mean s}
    [# avg {_moving s {toyAverage 0} {toyAverage 2} {toyAverage 1}}]
    [# at {_onLine {lerp 0.0 avg {smooth {phase s 13.3 14.0}}}}]
    {arrowLine "mean" {sub2 at {v2 0.0 1.05}} {sub2 at {v2 0.0 0.52}} estimateColor 3.0}]
Fn([], List(ScorePart)). The line, each list's dot as its sentence comes (list k at stage 8 + k, B B at 11), the
true total's mark from stage 12, circled in stage 19, the average's marker from 13, and the spread at the end.
$[# {_lineParts}
    [# {_dotPart k from} {part f"{dot${str k}}"
        {^ {s} {_dot k s}}
        {' {enterOver {+ from 0.4} 0.5 fadeIn}}}]
    {'
        {part "line"
            {^ {s} {numberLine "line" _lineRange _lineA _lineB textDimColor 0.32}}
            {' {enterOver 7.5 0.5 create}}}
        {_dotPart 0 8.0}
        {_dotPart 1 9.0}
        {_dotPart 2 11.0}
        {part "truth"
            {^ {s} {_truth}}
            {'
                {enterOver 12.0 0.7 create}
                {emphasize 18.6 19.0 {^ {t f} {circumscribe t f totalColor}}}}}
        {part "mean" _mean {' {enterOver 13.0 0.4 fadeIn}}}
        {part "spread" _spread {' {enterOver 22.2 0.6 fadeIn}}}}]

Phase three: W, and how often RIS keeps B

$[# _wCenter [% {v2 2.6 -0.1}]]
$[# {_wFormula} {moveTo
    {texParts "W" f"{W = \frac{\lit{1}{w_1 + w_2}}{\lit{2}{M}\,\lit{3}{\hat p(y)}}}" 0.55 textColor
        {' "sum" "M" "phat"}
        {' weightColor textColor targetColor}}
    _wCenter}]
Where the keeping formula sits: right of the line's labels, under W.
$[# _keepCenter [% {v2 5.0 -1.55}]]
$[# {_keepSymbols} {moveTo
    {texParts "keep" f"{\overline{W}_B = \frac{1}{\lit{1}{P(y = B)}}}" 0.45 textColor
        {' "chance"}
        {' estimateColor}}
    _keepCenter}]
$[# {_keepNumbers}
    [# k {toyKept 1}]
    {moveTo
        {texParts "keep" f"{\overline{W}_B = \frac{1}{\lit{1}{${numberLatex {.chance k} 1}}} = \lit{2}{${numberLatex {.w k} 1}}}" 0.45 textColor
            {' "chance" "value"}
            {' estimateColor weightColor}}
        _keepCenter}]
Fn([], List(Mob)). Where RIS keeps B: in each A-B cell, B's share of the two weights (12 of 12 + 4/3), and
all of B-B.
$[# {_keptB}
    [# cells {_cells "sq" weightColor}]
    [# wa {toyWeight 0 0}]
    [# wb {toyWeight 1 0}]
    [# share {/ wb {+ wa wb}}]
    [# {_part id along}
        [# b {boxOf {withId cells {++ "sq." id}}}]
        {!if along
            {filled
                {++ "keptB." id}
                {box {v2 {- {.x {.hi b}} {* share {boxWidth b}}} {.y {.lo b}}} {.hi b}}
                weightColor
                0.85}
            {filled
                {++ "keptB." id}
                {box {.lo b} {v2 {.x {.hi b}} {+ {.y {.lo b}} {* share {boxHeight b}}}}}
                weightColor
                0.85}}]
    {flatten {'
        {_part {_cell 0 1} false}
        {_part {_cell 1 0} true}
        {filled "keptB.1.1" {boxOf {withId cells {++ "sq." {_cell 1 1}}}} weightColor 0.85}}}]
Fn([Color], Fn([Float, List(Mob)], List(Mob))). A circle drawn around a figure in `color`, then faded (a mark).
$[# {_circled color} {^ {t f} {circumscribe t f color}}]
Fn([], List(Mob)). The braces naming W's parts: the sum of the weights, the count, and the kept one's target.
$[# {_braces}
    [# w {_wFormula}]
    [# {_under brace label toRight}
        [# b {boxOf brace}]
        [# l {nextTo label brace down 0.1}]
        {shift l {v2
            {!if toRight
                {- {+ {.x {.lo b}} {/ {widthOf l} 2.0}} {.x {centerOf l}}}
                {- {- {.x {.hi b}} {/ {widthOf l} 2.0}} {.x {centerOf l}}}}
            0.0}}]
    [# braceM {brace "braceM" {withId w "M"} down 0.1 textColor}]
    [# braceT {brace "braceT" {withId w "phat"} down 0.1 targetColor}]
    {flatten {'
        {braceLabel "braceSum"
            {withId w "sum"}
            up
            0.1
            weightColor
            {caption "braceSumText" {textKey "toymath-sum"} 0.34 weightColor}}
        braceM
        {_under braceM {caption "braceMText" {textKey "toymath-count"} 0.34 textColor} false}
        braceT
        {shift
            {_under braceT {caption "braceTText" {textKey "toymath-target"} 0.34 targetColor} true}
            {v2 0.0 -0.45}}}}]
Fn([], List(List(ScorePart))). Each list's parts: its cells lit, then their chances.
$[# {_lists} {' {_listParts 0 8.0} {_listParts 1 9.0} {_listParts 2 11.0}}]
Fn([], List(ScorePart)). The square and its lists (the chances drawn over where RIS keeps B), the formula from the symbols through each list's numbers and
the average to W, the chance RIS keeps B, and W's braces; all but the line leave at the end.
$[# {_formulaParts} {flatten {'
    {' {part "square" {^ {s} {_squareFigure}} {' {enterOver 7.5 0.5 create} {exit 22.0}}}}
    {map {_lists} head}
    {' {part "keptB" {^ {s} {_keptB}} {' {enter 17.0 create} {exit 22.0}}}}
    {map {_lists} {^ {l} {head {tail l}}}}
    {'
        {part "estimate"
            {^ {s} {_estimateSymbols}}
            {'
                {enterOver 7.6 0.4 fadeIn}
                {become 8.0 {^ {s} {_estimateNumbers 0}}}
                {become 9.0 {^ {s} {_estimateNumbers 1}}}
                {emphasize 10.0 11.0 {_circled targetColor}}
                {become 11.0 {^ {s} {_estimateNumbers 2}}}
                {become 13.0 {^ {s} {_averageFormula}}}
                {emphasize 14.0 15.0 {_circled totalColor}}
                {become 15.0 {^ {s} {_wFormula}}}
                {hold 18.0 19.0 {^ {t f} {crossParts t f {' "sum" "M"} weightColor}}}
                {exit 22.0}}}
        {part "keep"
            {^ {s} {_keepSymbols}}
            {'
                {enterOver 16.0 0.7 write}
                {becomeOver 17.3 0.7 {^ {s} {_keepNumbers}}}
                {exitOver 21.2 0.4 fadeOut}}}
        {part "braces" {^ {s} {_braces}} {' {enterOver 21.1 0.9 write} {exit 22.0}}}}}}]

The scene

The worked example as a score of 23 steps (`stepOf "toy" 23`, the clips below): the bars and the true total, the
table, the square of the lists with each list's estimate on the line, their average, and W; at the end the frame
closes on the line and the estimates' spread.
$[# {_toyScore} {score "toy" 23
    {flatten {'
        {_legendParts}
        {_barParts 0}
        {_barParts 1}
        {_totalParts}
        {_tableParts}
        {_formulaParts}
        {_lineParts}}}
    {'
        {frameKey 22.3 0.7 {^ {s} {frameOn
            {append {numberLine "line" _lineRange _lineA _lineB textDimColor 0.32} {_spread s}}
            0.5}}}}}]
$[# toyMath {: {^ {t} {playScore {_toyScore}}} Math}]

Clips

The scene's steps as clips (lab/src/clip.rs): its demonstration's Play plays every step in order, a second each;
the story plays each over its sentence's words, and sets the scene back to a step where a beat starts.
$[# toySteps [% {stepsInOrder "toy" 23}]]
$[# toyAt0 [% {stepsAt "toy" 23 0}]]
$[# toyStep1 [% {stepClip "toy" 1 0.0 1.0}]]
